1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:16,379
[Host] Welcome to Japanese Daily News. I'm Maya. Today is June nineteenth. Japan is changing the rules for private lodging — renting out homes to travelers — after a rise in trouble with the neighbors. Let's listen.

2
00:00:16,980 --> 00:00:19,739
[News] 今日のニュースです。

3
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:28,719
[News] 「民泊」は、ふつうの家やマンションに、旅行者をお金をもらって泊めることです。

4
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:36,692
[News] 外国から来る旅行者が増えて、民泊を使う人も多くなりました。

5
00:00:37,392 --> 00:00:42,648
[News] でも、近所の人とのトラブルも増えています。

6
00:00:43,347 --> 00:00:50,524
[News] 夜おそくまでうるさかったり、ゴミの出し方が悪かったりするからです。

7
00:00:51,223 --> 00:00:58,207
[News] 知らない人が家の近くを歩くので、こわいと感じる人もいます。

8
00:00:58,908 --> 00:01:05,028
[News] そこで、観光庁は、ルールを変えることにしました。

9
00:01:05,727 --> 00:01:14,248
[News] これからは、市や町が、住宅が多い場所で民泊を強く制限できます。

10
00:01:14,947 --> 00:01:22,459
[News] 旅行者を泊めてもよい日を、一年でとても少なくすることもできます。

11
00:01:23,159 --> 00:01:31,823
[News] 観光庁は、旅行者も近所の人も、安心できるようにしたいと話しています。

12
00:01:32,524 --> 00:01:34,156
[Host] Let's break it down.

13
00:01:34,756 --> 00:01:44,212
[Slow] 「民泊」は、ふつうの家やマンションに、旅行者をお金をもらって泊めることです。

14
00:01:45,012 --> 00:01:50,531
[Host] The word here means putting travelers up in an ordinary house or apartment for money.

15
00:01:51,132 --> 00:01:53,555
[Vocab] 民泊

16
00:01:53,956 --> 00:02:03,555
[Host] It means private lodging — renting out a regular home to travelers, the way home-sharing apps work. The two characters mean 'people' and 'stay.'

17
00:02:04,156 --> 00:02:12,460
[Slow] 外国から来る旅行者が増えて、民泊を使う人も多くなりました。

18
00:02:13,259 --> 00:02:18,683
[Host] As more travelers come from abroad, more people are using private lodging too.

19
00:02:19,283 --> 00:02:21,756
[Vocab] 旅行者

20
00:02:22,156 --> 00:02:29,788
[Host] It means a traveler. The first part means travel, and the last character means person — so, a travel-person.

21
00:02:30,388 --> 00:02:36,388
[Slow] でも、近所の人とのトラブルも増えています。

22
00:02:37,187 --> 00:02:40,331
[Host] But trouble with the neighbors is also increasing.

23
00:02:40,931 --> 00:02:43,092
[Vocab] 近所

24
00:02:43,491 --> 00:02:49,276
[Host] It means the neighborhood, or nearby — the people and houses just around you.

25
00:02:49,876 --> 00:02:58,060
[Slow] 夜おそくまでうるさかったり、ゴミの出し方が悪かったりするからです。

26
00:02:58,860 --> 00:03:04,379
[Host] That's because of things like being noisy late at night, or not putting the trash out properly.

27
00:03:04,979 --> 00:03:07,211
[Vocab] うるさい

28
00:03:07,611 --> 00:03:15,075
[Host] It means noisy or loud. Used about a person, it can also mean fussy. Here it's loud guests late at night.

29
00:03:15,675 --> 00:03:23,644
[Slow] 知らない人が家の近くを歩くので、こわいと感じる人もいます。

30
00:03:24,443 --> 00:03:28,883
[Host] Because strangers walk near their homes, some people feel scared.

31
00:03:29,484 --> 00:03:31,788
[Vocab] 感じる

32
00:03:32,187 --> 00:03:40,036
[Host] It means to feel or sense something. To feel uneasy, to feel cold, to feel scared — all use this verb.

33
00:03:40,635 --> 00:03:47,620
[Slow] そこで、観光庁は、ルールを変えることにしました。

34
00:03:48,419 --> 00:03:52,596
[Host] So the Japan Tourism Agency decided to change the rules.

35
00:03:53,195 --> 00:03:55,355
[Vocab] 変える

36
00:03:55,756 --> 00:04:03,747
[Host] It means to change something — change the rules, change your plans. The verb for something changing on its own is a different word.

37
00:04:04,348 --> 00:04:14,092
[Slow] これからは、市や町が、住宅が多い場所で民泊を強く制限できます。

38
00:04:14,891 --> 00:04:21,732
[Host] From now on, cities and towns can strongly restrict private lodging in areas with lots of homes.

39
00:04:22,331 --> 00:04:24,708
[Vocab] 制限

40
00:04:25,108 --> 00:04:32,860
[Host] It means a limit or restriction — a cap on what's allowed. Here, a cap on lodging in residential areas.

41
00:04:33,459 --> 00:04:42,052
[Slow] 旅行者を泊めてもよい日を、一年でとても少なくすることもできます。

42
00:04:42,851 --> 00:04:47,723
[Host] They can even cut the number of days per year travelers may be put up to very few.

43
00:04:48,324 --> 00:04:50,411
[Vocab] 泊める

44
00:04:50,812 --> 00:04:57,963
[Host] It means to put someone up for the night, to give them lodging. A related verb means to stay overnight yourself.

45
00:04:58,564 --> 00:05:01,564
[Host] Let's listen to the full story one more time.

46
00:05:02,163 --> 00:05:04,923
[News] 今日のニュースです。

47
00:05:05,624 --> 00:05:13,903
[News] 「民泊」は、ふつうの家やマンションに、旅行者をお金をもらって泊めることです。

48
00:05:14,603 --> 00:05:21,875
[News] 外国から来る旅行者が増えて、民泊を使う人も多くなりました。

49
00:05:22,576 --> 00:05:27,831
[News] でも、近所の人とのトラブルも増えています。

50
00:05:28,531 --> 00:05:35,708
[News] 夜おそくまでうるさかったり、ゴミの出し方が悪かったりするからです。

51
00:05:36,408 --> 00:05:43,391
[News] 知らない人が家の近くを歩くので、こわいと感じる人もいます。

52
00:05:44,091 --> 00:05:50,211
[News] そこで、観光庁は、ルールを変えることにしました。

53
00:05:50,911 --> 00:05:59,432
[News] これからは、市や町が、住宅が多い場所で民泊を強く制限できます。

54
00:06:00,132 --> 00:06:07,644
[News] 旅行者を泊めてもよい日を、一年でとても少なくすることもできます。

55
00:06:08,343 --> 00:06:17,007
[News] 観光庁は、旅行者も近所の人も、安心できるようにしたいと話しています。

56
00:06:17,708 --> 00:06:20,444
[Host] Quiz time. Three questions.

57
00:06:21,043 --> 00:06:25,100
[Slow] 「民泊」とは、何ですか。

58
00:06:25,899 --> 00:06:30,795
[Host] What is 'minpaku'? Putting travelers up in an ordinary home for money.

59
00:06:31,396 --> 00:06:37,012
[Slow] 民泊で、どんなトラブルが増えていますか。

60
00:06:37,812 --> 00:06:44,843
[Host] What kind of trouble is increasing with private lodging? Noise and badly handled trash that bother the neighbors.

61
00:06:45,444 --> 00:06:50,915
[Slow] これから、市や町は何ができますか。

62
00:06:51,716 --> 00:06:58,172
[Host] What will cities and towns be able to do? Strongly restrict private lodging in residential areas.

63
00:06:58,771 --> 00:07:11,156
[Host] That's today's Japanese Daily News. Full transcript with furigana at podcast.jpnotes.dev. Subscribe on Apple Podcasts or Spotify. See you tomorrow.

64
00:07:11,755 --> 00:07:14,012
[News] また明日。
